      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:38:39Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(import): the STEP facet budget is a setting carried with the import\n\nThe STEP importer's facet budget (the constant MAX_FACETS) becomes a\nvalue an import carries: ImportModel::within(path, budget), the script\nverb cam.import(path, name?, facetBudget?) and MCP import_model's\noptional facet_budget. The default is today's 30M cap, so no default\nimport changes; a budget outside 1000..=60000000, or one given for an\nSTL/OBJ file, is refused by name before parsing.\n\nThe budget a mesh was made under is recorded with the model\n(schema::StepBudget, only when not the default) and traded with the\nfacets by import, update, repair, delete and their undo; the project\nfile keeps it as an optional facet_budget key (absent = default, so\nolder files load unchanged; out of bounds is refused at load). get_job\nand cam.import report it. The reduced-fidelity flag is computed exactly\nas before: a smaller budget flags, a larger one clears on re-import.\nThe refusal text now names the setting (\"a larger STEP facet budget\").\n\nGUI: the model page carries a \"STEP facet budget (next import)\" row,\nrefused by name out of bounds, read by every STEP import the window\nstarts.\n\nFixes #1054\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
